# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Maksim Kulichenko et al. (2023). Uncertainty-driven dynamics for active learning of interatomic potentials.
#   Nature Computational Science. doi:10.1038/s43588-023-00406-5
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 e4e317d2dbf060bd...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 130 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the uncertainty-driven dynamics active-learning scheme
# (MD biased towards regions of high ensemble uncertainty) demonstrated
# with ANI potentials for glycine. Four ANI models are compared, trained
# on data sets collected by UDD-AL at 350 K and by plain MD-AL at 350,
# 600 and 1,000 K; their architecture and training settings are encoded.
# Errors on the 50 ns test set are given as a bound and in figures.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
