###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Final models: on average 695 training epochs at about 0.098 s per epoch
# on NVIDIA TITAN V GPUs (trainingHardware on the UDD-AL model; the
# statement covers all final models).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Accuracy on the 50 ns MD test set is stated as an energy RMSE 'of less than 0.3 kcal/mol' for all models, with the 350 K MD-AL model about 0.11 kcal/mol lower than the others; no value per model is printed, so no AccuracyMetric is encoded. The errors along conformational scans (proton transfer, rotations, bond scans) are figures.
# - The radial cutoff (4.6 A, 32 shifts) is encoded as cutoffRadius and the angular cutoff (3.5 A) as angularCutoff; the descriptor has 768 elements for four atom types.
# - The acetylacetone demonstration uses the pretrained ANI-1x model (the model of smith2018) in MD; it is not encoded because no result is attached to it.
# - The uncertainty bias itself (magnitude and width of the bias potential) has no place in schema 0.1.2. Software for the ANI training is not named in the parts read.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
